{
	title: 'Session ids sort by day and hour',
	spec: "A new session's id is '<day>-<word>'. day: whole days since this home's epoch, an ISO time in state/epoch.ason written by the first session (old Hal's epoch can be copied in to keep its numbering), padded to two digits. word: from src/host/session-words.txt, a sorted list of three-letter words without crude or charged ones, cut into 24 equal slots by local hour, so a day's ids list in roughly creation order (mornings early in the alphabet, evenings late). Up to three tries come from this hour's slot, two more from it and its neighbors, five from the whole list, then three random letters; the directory is claimed by non-recursive mkdir. An invalid epoch throws. sessions.newest() picks, among the highest day with a readable session, the latest createdAt. No tests for the id choice.",
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		"The day rolls over at the epoch's time of day, not midnight (old Hal's epoch: 10:09 UTC), as in old Hal; kept for numbering continuity. Pruned from old Hal's words3.txt: bra cia dem die fat fbi gay god gop gun hiv ira irs nam pee sex sin tit war."
